description: Continue a previous session — read context and pick up where you left off
---

## Current State

- Git status: !`git status --short | head -5`
- Current branch: !`git branch --show-current`
- Recent commits: !`git log --oneline -3`

## Resume Protocol

Read the following files in order, then continue working on the next priority item:

1. `CLAUDE.md` — project rules and conventions
2. `.claude/SERVICE_CONTEXT.md` — current project state (if it exists)
3. `.claude/NEXT_STEPS.md` — what to work on next (if it exists)
4. `.claude/KNOWN_ISSUES.md` — issues to be aware of (if it exists)
5. `tasks/session-summary.md` — last session's handoff notes (if it exists)
6. `tasks/current-state.md` — cycle progress (if autonomous loop was running)

After reading, identify the highest-priority item and begin working on it. Track progress in `tasks/todo.md`.
